{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976474-create-a-condition-or-tilt","id":976474,"title":"Create a Condition (or Tilt)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T05:07:28-07:00","id":976474,"title":"Create a Condition (or Tilt)","content":"I am a fan of the Fate Core system, my go-to system for games that are more &quot;pulp&quot; and heroic than the average CofD game. I like the Create and Advantage action you can perform in that system; you use one skill to create an advantage for yourself in order to improve your chances at another roll. This effectively simulates how certain skills work well together, and it also allows non-combat characters to be of more use in combats because a creative player can use social and mental skills to create advantages for a more combat-focused character.<br /> <br /> Does this have a clear analog in CofD? I know you can cause Tilts in combat, but is there also a Condition-generating system in place that I have blundered past or is such a thing implied and assumed throughout the rules?<br /> <br /> Take the Informed Condition for example, can a character simply sit down and read up on a subject, reach a certain amount of successes set by the Storyteller and then gain the Condition or are conditions like these only meant as gravy if you gain an exceptional success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:03:32-07:00","id":976614,"title":"","content":"Mage has some great guidelines for creating custom Conditions and Tilts, might be worth a look. As for acquiring Conditions, exceptional success is the default method, but lots of specific abilities cause Conditions, and there's also always ST fiat. So you can certainly allow players to grant themselves Conditions with other actions, FATE-style if you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T14:57:14-07:00","id":976740,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I just read the Mage guidelines on Conditions and it gave me some good insights. I now have another question: is it a hard rule to give beats for Conditions? Even purely beneficial ones, not just those that require some effort or inconvenience from the character, such as Shaken and Spooked? The Chronicles of Darkness make it seem so and now Mage as well, I am quite fond of handing out Conditions for all kinds of events and things that players do, if I apply that rule my players will be superheroes in short order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 09-26-2016, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:19:22-07:00","id":976753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976474-create-a-condition-or-tilt?p=976740#post976740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I just read the Mage guidelines on Conditions and it gave me some good insights. I now have another question: is it a hard rule to give beats for Conditions? Even purely beneficial ones, not just those that require some effort or inconvenience from the character, such as Shaken and Spooked? The Chronicles of Darkness make it seem so and now Mage as well, I am quite fond of handing out Conditions for all kinds of events and things that players do, if I apply that rule my players will be superheroes in short order.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, beneficial Conditions only give a Beat on Resolution. One way to side step that is to give them a way to &quot;lapse&quot;, get removed, or fade away without Resolution - then, since they didn't Resolve, no Beat. Another method is to offer some incentive for characters spending Beats on other things than Experiences - I think you can cash in a Beat for a Willpower, in Core? Give the PCs alternative options. Then, they must choose between spending them for immediate benefit, or saving them for long term growth.<br /> <br /> Options (no idea how balanced these are):<ul><li>Downgrade a point of damage</li> <li>+1 to a roll (max +5)</li> <li>&quot;Temporary&quot; Merit (goes away after a scene or a day - cost is dots in Beats)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-26-2016, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:20:07-07:00","id":976754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976474-create-a-condition-or-tilt?p=976740#post976740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I just read the Mage guidelines on Conditions and it gave me some good insights. I now have another question: is it a hard rule to give beats for Conditions? Even purely beneficial ones, not just those that require some effort or inconvenience from the character, such as Shaken and Spooked? The Chronicles of Darkness make it seem so and now Mage as well, I am quite fond of handing out Conditions for all kinds of events and things that players do, if I apply that rule my players will be superheroes in short order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conditions always grant Beats when Resolved, yes, even purely beneficial ones. However, you can only recieve up to one Beat from a given source per Scene. So, if you resolve 3 Conditions in the same Scene, you still only get one Beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}